\section{Block separator}
\label{sec:block-sep}

A commit message can hold several run blocks separated by a line
of three dashes surrounded by blank lines.
Current learnlog versions write one run per commit, but this
layout is still what a reader meets: repositories recorded by
older versions grouped consecutive runs of unchanged code into
one message, ProgSnap2 reconstruction rebuilds a commit from
however many runs it has (\cref{progsnap2}), and joining a run's
trailer back onto its header (\cref{sec:run-join}) produces
exactly that block again.
This separator is safe to split on because the section markers
within a run block ([[--- I/O ---]], [[--- exception ---]])
always have additional text after the dashes.

We define it here rather than in the CLI module because both
the commit functions and the ProgSnap2 exporter need it.

<<commits constants>>=
BLOCK_SEP = "\n\n---\n\n"
@


\section{Joining a run's two commits}
\label{sec:run-join}

A run is recorded as a header commit and a later trailer commit
that names it by run id (\cref{sec:two-commit-protocol}).
That split exists to make \emph{writing} safe under interleaving;
nobody reading a log wants to see it.
Every reader below therefore works with \emph{records}: a header
commit whose message has its trailer merged back in, which is
byte-for-byte the run block that a finalised run used to be.
Trailer commits themselves are dropped from the listings---they
carry no code state and no new command, only the results of a run
that is already in the list.

Joining takes three steps: recognising a trailer commit,
collecting all trailers by run id, and merging a trailer into the
header block that asks for it.

\subsection{Recognising a trailer commit}

A trailer commit is identified by its subject keyword, and its
body starts with the run id it completes.
Everything after that line is the trailer text as
[[format_run_trailer]] produced it, so recovering it is a matter
of dropping the two lines that the commit added.

<<commits functions>>=
def parse_trailer_message(message):
    """Split a trailer commit message.

    Returns ``(run_id, trailer_text)``, or ``None`` when
    ``message`` is not a trailer commit.
    """
    if not message or not message.startswith(TRAILER_PREFIX):
        return None

    lines = message.split("\n")
    for index, line in enumerate(lines):
        if line.startswith(RUN_ID_FIELD):
            run_id = line[len(RUN_ID_FIELD):].strip()
            trailer = "\n".join(
                lines[index + 1:]
            ).strip("\n")
            return run_id, trailer
    return None
@

<<commits test functions>>=
def test_parse_trailer_message():
    from learnlog.commits import parse_trailer_message
    message = (
        "Run-End: hello.py (none)\n"
        "\n"
        "Run-Id: abc123\n"
        "End-Time: 2026-01-01T10:00:05\n"
        "Exit-Code: 0\n"
    )
    run_id, trailer = parse_trailer_message(message)
    assert run_id == "abc123"
    assert trailer.startswith("End-Time:")
    assert "Run-Id" not in trailer

def test_parse_trailer_message_rejects_header():
    from learnlog.commits import parse_trailer_message
    assert parse_trailer_message(
        "Run: hello.py (none)\n\nScript: hello.py\n"
    ) is None
    assert parse_trailer_message("") is None
